# ============================================================================
# THE ARCHIVE (14 Aug 2026 — ARCHIVE__DAY_ONE_SPEC.md §7.5)
# The permanent record lives OUTSIDE the repo by design ($ARSENAL_ARCHIVE,
# default %USERPROFILE%\CyborgArchive) and `archivist.mjs init` REFUSES to
# create it inside a git work tree. These lines are the second belt: if a bag
# ever appears in here — a copy pulled back off the disk to inspect, a mistyped
# $ARSENAL_ARCHIVE, a restore into the wrong folder — git must not see it.
# The repo is PUBLIC and a push cannot be taken back.
# Third belt: hooks/pre-commit (installed by setup\INSTALL_ARCHIVE.ps1) refuses
# any staged file inside a BagIt bag, and any capture lane git has never tracked.
# Reversal: delete these lines. Nothing reads them from the remote.
CyborgArchive/
**/CyborgArchive/
bagit.txt
bag-info.txt
manifest-sha256.txt
tagmanifest-sha256.txt

# Git Bash crash dumps. Zero value, and one untracked file is enough to make
# audit.mjs REFUSE to run (its dirty-tree guard, audit.mjs:103) — which is how
# the `audit` lane went 52h stale while looking like a scheduling problem.
# Ignored rather than deleted: it is a crash artifact, not anyone's work.
*.stackdump

